---
/**
 * The strip of labelled facts along the bottom of a reference card, as the
 * schema definitions on `/api/schema` and the MCP tools in `docs/mcp-tools.mdx`
 * both want it: a fixed label column with its values beside it.
 *
 * Pass `<dt>`/`<dd>` pairs. It carries no facts of its own, so what a reference
 * calls its facts stays that reference's business while the chrome — the
 * rounded-off footer, the label column, the rhythm between rows — is decided
 * once. `ConfigParam` and `ErrorCode` deliberately do not use it: a run of short
 * `flag`/`env`/`default` pairs reads better inline than in a column, and an
 * error's hint is one sentence rather than a list.
 */
---
<footer
    class="-mx-4 -mb-3.5 rounded-b-inner border-t bg-muted px-4 py-2 text-sm text-muted-foreground"
>
    <dl class="grid grid-cols-[4.5rem_minmax(0,1fr)] gap-x-3 gap-y-0.5 code-plain">
        <slot />
    </dl>
</footer>
